## Notes

### System-Specific Notes

**Novel-OS (Creative Writing)**:
- **Direct Commands** (`/plan-novel`, `/create-outline`, etc.) provide instant creative workflow execution
- **Command Files** in `~/.claude/commands/` map to workflow instructions in `~/.novel-os/instructions/core/`
- **Writing Standards** in `~/.novel-os/standards/` ensure consistent, high-quality creative writing
- All guides emphasize **narrative coherence** and **compelling storytelling**
- **Genre guides** provide specialized writing approaches for different fiction types
- Novel-OS workflows focus on **creative development** and **manuscript management**

**Agent-OS (Software Development)**:
- **Direct Commands** (`/plan-product`, `/create-spec`, etc.) provide instant development workflow execution
- **Command Files** in `~/.agent-os/commands/` map to workflow instructions in `~/.agent-os/instructions/core/`
- **Development Standards** ensure consistent, high-quality code across all implementations
- All guides emphasize **simplicity** and **minimum viable implementation**
- **Performance** and **security** considerations are built into every guide
- **Accessibility** requirements are included in frontend guides
- Agent-OS workflows focus on **product development** and **feature implementation**

### General Notes

- **System Detection**: Claude Code automatically detects whether to use Novel-OS or Agent-OS based on the command used
- **Workflow Isolation**: Novel-OS and Agent-OS are completely separate systems with different purposes
- **Command Clarity**: Each system has distinct commands that don't overlap
- When in doubt, choose the **simpler solution** over the complex one
- **Commands provide the fastest way** for users to invoke specific workflows